# Cast four illusion spells, try to pick up each illusory item, and photograph
# what the game says. Read by tools/check_illusion_flags.sh. Bead inc-pu6v.43.
#
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat \
#   INCURSION_LOAD=tools/fixtures/chars/elf-mage-illusions-seed1.sav \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/illusion-flags.keys 1
#
# THE ORACLE is Creature::PickUp (src/Inv.cpp:496-505), which prints one of two
# lines and never both:
#
#   isRealTo false -> "You can't pick up an illusionary item."
#   isRealTo true  -> "As you reach to pick up the <Obj>, your hand passes
#                      through it, and it winks out of existence!"
#
# The caster is the watcher, and that is legal here: the illusory-ITEM arm of
# Magic::Illusion (src/Effects.cpp:1969-1973) grants the caster no DISBELIEVED
# stati, unlike the illusory-CREATURE arm (src/Encounter.cpp:2551). So the elf
# gets a genuine isRealTo verdict on an illusion he cast himself.
#
# THE FOUR SPELLS are a ladder, one level apart, and their declared flags
# alternate. That is the whole design: the save DC rises by exactly 1 per rung
# while the declared IL_IMPROVED flag does not, so any code that reads the flag
# out of the DC must disagree with the declaration on some rung.
#
#   spell                       level  DC  yval                     improved?
#   Phantasmal Force              1    15  0                        no
#   Improved Phantasmal Force     2    16  IL_IMPROVED              YES
#   Spectral Force                3    17  IL_SPECTRAL              no
#   Improved Spectral Force       4    18  IL_SPECTRAL|IL_IMPROVED  YES
#
# The DCs are this fixture's, measured: getSpellDC is 10 + level + attribute
# modifier + school focus (src/Magic.cpp:3334-3396), and for this elf that is
# 14 + level. The check does not hard-code them; it asserts the MESSAGES, which
# follow from the declared flags alone and hold at every DC.
#
# THE DUMP LABELS are il-a..il-d rather than the spell names, because a glob
# of "*-phantasmal-force" also matches "*-improved-phantasmal-force" and the
# check would then read two screens where it meant one.
#
# ONE STEP EAST BETWEEN CASTS. An illusion that is refused stays on the floor,
# and a second item in the same square would turn the next 'g' into a menu.
# The illusion is placed at the caster's own feet, so moving moves the target.
#
# SPACE, NEVER ESC, to clear the "-- more --" prompt. In play mode ESC opens
# the System Menu, whose [a] is Save and Quit; a stray ESC ends the run and
# still exits 0.

@dump:arrival

@until "Select Spell" m
@choose "Phantasmal Force"
i
@expect "Target Illusion"
ENTER
SPACE
g
@dump:il-a-plain
SPACE SPACE
RIGHT

@until "Select Spell" m
@choose "Improved Phantasmal Fo"
i
@expect "Target Illusion"
ENTER
SPACE
g
@dump:il-b-improved
SPACE SPACE
RIGHT

@until "Select Spell" m
@choose "Spectral Force"
i
@expect "Target Illusion"
ENTER
SPACE
g
@dump:il-c-spectral
SPACE SPACE
RIGHT

@until "Select Spell" m
@choose "Improved Spectral Force"
i
@expect "Target Illusion"
ENTER
SPACE
g
@dump:il-d-spectral-improved
